# Bellbound Monk CT02 — supernatural animation tests

Two clean-ink, elevated three-quarter experiments for Lantern. These are native-resolution animation tests in one heading, not a rig or a completed multidirectional game implementation.

## Motion

- **Buoyant pendulum locomotion:** six drawings, 48 ticks at 60 Hz (0.8 seconds), looping. Short levitation, whole-body compression/puff, delayed robe swing and a heavy bell pendulum. Drawing holds: 8, 7, 10, 7, 6, 10 ticks.
- **Concussive bell toll:** eight drawings, 72 ticks at 60 Hz (1.2 seconds), one-shot. Draw-in, loaded back-coil, sharp downward toll, broad stylized shockwave, recoil and heavy settle. Drawing holds: 8, 9, 12, 3, 6, 5, 12, 17 ticks. The attack's anticipation ends at tick29; the widest wave starts at tick32. These are animation timing cues, not implemented damage or collision events.

The videos repeat clips for review. The cast's runtime loop flag is false. They are genuine 60 fps encoded previews using held drawings, not 60 unique drawings per second and not optical-flow interpolation. Locomotion video:192 encoded frames /3.2s. Cast video:216 encoded frames /3.6s.

