## Registration and native pixels

Every runtime cel is640×576 with fixed root/pivot(320,500) measured from top-left. For an engine with bottom-left normalized pivots, use(0.5,0.1319444444). Empty padding is intentionally generous. The origins remain fixed; no cel is fitted to its subject or rescaled. Source grid origins were rounded to integer pixels for lossless registration. Cross-clip native scale is close but not a physically calibrated character height.

Ownership crop boundaries sometimes move within empty source gutters because robe/bell or wave silhouettes extend past the nominal generated cell boundary. This does not move the drawing: all pixels are registered against fixed source grid anchors, not silhouette centers. Disconnected gold wave arcs in cast5–6 are retained. Validation confirms every nonzero alpha pixel in each cleaned source ownership region survives in its output cel; all cels have safe margins and no neighboring artwork.

Source files are unchanged. Runtime processing clamps alpha≤16 to0 and alpha≥250 to255, retains intermediate antialiasing and does not repaint RGB, add pixels, scale, rotate, warp or upscale artwork.

## Camera and limits

The requested camera is orthographic elevation35.2643896828°, world azimuth45°, actor facing world+X / screen-down-right30°. The generated cels visibly expose hood crowns, shoulder tops, bell top planes and shoes. The painted projection is a visually audited approximation; prompts and reference diagrams do not prove exact geometric projection. No additional facings, mirrors, engine-scale capture or engine integration are included.

All fourteen cels preserve a stout ochre-robed monk, charcoal cowl/cuffs/gloves, smooth blank oval brass mask, two hands and one large bell. Cloth and body volume deliberately squash and swell. Some cel-to-cel robe proportions and the small locomotion wrap-pop remain visible in this low-drawing-count test. The bell is visually coherent but not generated from one mechanically locked3D solid. Gold shockwaves remain baked into cast cels; they are not separate engine VFX. Lighting and hand overlap require a separate review before mirroring.

